              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">T16</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,999, free shipping</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$2,150.00</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Bowflex is $151 cheaper before delivery</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">BXT8J</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not sold</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,123.72</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Costs more than a T6 this week</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Treadmill 10 (discontinued)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not sold</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$2,999.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,000 above its $1,999 list price when sold</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Treadmill 7 (discontinued)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not sold</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$2,499.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$800 above Academy’s $1,699.99 on 20 Oct</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Treadmill 22 (discontinued)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not sold</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Listed, no price shown</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not available to buy</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>The T16 is cheaper direct.</strong> $1,999 with free shipping on bowflex.com against
            $2,150.00 on Amazon. The only reason to buy it on Amazon this week would be a delivery or return term
            you prefer, and Bowflex’s offer ends on 26 November, after which the gap may close or widen.</li>
            <li><strong>The discontinued models are priced above their history.</strong> Our <a href="/bowflex-treadmill-10/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Treadmill 10 page</a> records a $1,999 US list price when it was sold,
            and academy.com showed the Treadmill 10 at $2,299.00 and the Treadmill 7 at $1,699.99 on 20 October
            2026. Amazon’s $2,999.99 and $2,499.99 are above both.</li>
            <li><strong>The BXT8J is an older-style model</strong> with a 20 by 60-inch belt and 15% incline
            on its listing. At $1,123.72 it costs $224.72 more than the T6’s Black Friday price, for a machine
            whose listing does not give its weight rating or warranty.</li>
            <li><strong>Check the seller.</strong> Bowflex’s price match promise excludes third-party
            marketplace sellers, and warranty support is simplest when the seller is Bowflex or an authorised
            retailer. Register the machine with Bowflex wherever you buy it.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div id="vs-other-brands" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Bowflex vs Horizon and Sole at Black Friday Prices</h2>
<p>
            Horizon, Bowflex’s sister brand at Johnson Health Tech, and Sole are the brands most Bowflex buyers
            also look at, and both are running Black Friday pricing to the same 27 November deadline. Using
            their prices on 23 November 2026, from our <a href="/horizon-treadmill-black-friday-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Horizon Black Friday deals</a> and <a href="/sole-treadmill-black-friday-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Sole Black Friday deals</a> pages:
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[620px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Price band</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Bowflex (24 Nov)</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Horizon (23 Nov)</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Sole (23 Nov)</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">The trade-off</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">About $900 to $1,100</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">T6, $899</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">7.0 AT, $934 with code</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">F63, $1,099.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">All 20 x 60 in. and 12 mph; the T6 is the cheapest of the three</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">About $1,400 to $1,500</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">T9, $1,399</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">7.4 AT, $1,499 with code</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">F80, $1,499.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">The T9 and 7.4 AT both have 22-inch decks and 350 lb ratings; the T9 is $100 less</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">About $1,800 to $2,000</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">T16, $1,999</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">7.8 AT, $1,799 with code</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">F85, $1,999.99</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">All 22 x 60 in.; the T16 and F85 have large touchscreens, the 7.8 AT a colour screen and a 375 lb rating</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            The comparison favours Bowflex at the bottom and middle of the range this week: the T6 undercuts
            the 7.0 AT by $35 and the T9 undercuts the <a href="/horizon-7-4-at-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>7.4 AT</a> by $100. Warranties differ, though. Bowflex gives
            three years of parts and one of labour on all three; Horizon gives three years of parts on the
            7.0 AT and five years of parts and two of labour on the 7.4 AT and 7.8 AT; Sole states lifetime frame
            and motor cover across its range. Horizon also needs a code this week, and Bowflex does not.
          </p>
          <p>
            At the top, Bowflex’s T16 is the dearest of the three on the sticker, but its free shipping narrows
            the gap. If you want the touchscreen, the T16 and Sole F85 are within a dollar of each other; if
            you do not, the Horizon 7.8 AT is $200 less with the same 375 lb rating. For the iFIT-based
            alternative, see the <a href="/nordictrack-black-friday-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">NordicTrack Black Friday deals</a> page.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="when-to-buy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>When to Buy: Before the Deadline, or Wait?</h2>
<p>
            The T16’s offer ends at 11:59 pm Central on Thursday 26 November; the T6’s and T9’s at 11:59 pm
            Central on Friday 27 November. Cyber Monday is 30 November 2026. There are three reasonable
            approaches.
          </p>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>Buy the T6 or T9 this week if it is the one you want.</strong> $899 and $1,399 are the
            lowest prices we have recorded for them, and Bowflex put the T9 back up to $1,499 within a week of
            charging $1,399 in October. There is no guarantee these prices return quickly.</li>
            <li><strong>Do not rush the T16 on price alone.</strong> $1,999 is above its October sale price,
            and only the free shipping makes it level. If you want it, buy by 26 November for the free
            shipping; if you are unsure, waiting costs you little more than the delivery charge.</li>
            <li><strong>If you miss the deadline, check again on Cyber Monday</strong>, and judge any price
            against the table on this page. Our <a href="/cyber-monday-treadmill-deals/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Cyber Monday treadmill deals</a> page covers what usually
            changes between Friday and Monday.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>
            We have no information on Bowflex’s stock levels or ship dates beyond the products showing as
            available to order on 24 November. If you need the treadmill by a particular day, confirm the
            delivery window with Bowflex’s sales team before you pay. If you are not in a hurry, our guide to
            the <a href="/best-time-of-year-to-buy-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">best time of year to buy a treadmill</a> covers the
            other sale windows.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="checklist" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Before You Click Buy: A Bowflex Checklist</h2>
<ul>
            <li><strong>Measure the space.</strong> Bowflex gives assembled dimensions of 76 by 35 by 71 inches
            for the T6 and 77.2 by 37 by 67.6 inches for the T9 and T16, folding to 44 and 48.6 inches long
            respectively. Leave clear space behind the deck as well.</li>
            <li><strong>Check the ceiling.</strong> Bowflex’s minimum ceiling height for all three is your
            height plus 20.75 inches. At 15% incline you stand higher still at the front of the deck, so allow
            extra if the ceiling is close.</li>
            <li><strong>Plan the power.</strong> Treadmills draw a lot of current, and our <a href="/bowflex-treadmill-troubleshooting/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Bowflex troubleshooting</a> guide covers the power
            problems that follow sharing a circuit or using an extension lead. Read the electrical
            requirements in the manual before delivery day.</li>
            <li><strong>Confirm the model.</strong> The T9 and T16 share a frame and look alike in some
            photos. Check the console (7-inch LCD or 16-inch touchscreen) and the weight rating in your
            basket.</li>
            <li><strong>Price delivery and the plan separately.</strong> Compare the delivered total, with the
            delivery tier you need, not the sticker price.</li>
            <li><strong>Screenshot the price and date.</strong> If something goes wrong with the order, a dated
            record of the offer is the quickest way to sort it out.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            For the brand as a whole, including how Bowflex’s range has changed since Johnson Health Tech took
            over, see our <a href="/bowflex/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Bowflex treadmills guide</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Common mistakes -->
        <div id="common-mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Buying a Bowflex at Black Friday? Avoid These 4 Mistakes</h2>
          <p>Bowflex’s sale is simple, with no codes to remember. These four still catch buyers out.</p>
          <ol class="ed-mistakes not-prose">
            <li>
              <h3>Measuring the deal against the regular price</h3>
              <p>Bowflex’s regular prices of $1,299, $1,799 and $2,299 are not what it usually charges. The T6 was $899 and the T9 $1,399 in October as well, so judge the Black Friday price against the earlier sale prices on this page.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Missing the T16’s earlier deadline</h3>
              <p>The T16 offer ends at 11:59 pm Central on 26 November, Thanksgiving, a day before the T6 and T9. If the free shipping matters to you, order by Thursday, not Friday.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Assuming every model ships free</h3>
              <p>Only the T16’s offer includes free shipping. On the T6 and T9, standard delivery was $99, room of choice $249 and white glove $349 on 24 November, so add the tier you need before comparing.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Buying a discontinued Bowflex on Amazon because the name is familiar</h3>
              <p>The Treadmill 10 at $2,999.99 and Treadmill 7 at $2,499.99 on Amazon are priced well above what they sold for new. A current T9 or T16 from bowflex.com costs less this week.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- The bottom line -->
        <div id="bottom-line" class="ed-bottomline">
          <h2>The bottom line</h2>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">Bowflex’s Black Friday prices are honest but familiar.</strong> On
            24 November 2026 bowflex.com had the T6 at $899 and the T9 at $1,399 until 27 November, and the T16
            at $1,999 with free shipping until 26 November, with no code needed. The T6 and T9 prices are the
            lowest we have recorded but match mid-October; the T16 is about level with October once delivery is
            counted.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">Buy direct, and buy the right model.</strong> Amazon is dearer on the
            T16 and does not sell the T6 or T9, and its discontinued Bowflex listings are priced above their
            history. For most buyers the T6 is the deal to take; for runners, the T9. See our <a href="/how-much-does-a-bowflex-treadmill-cost/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Bowflex price guide</a> and <a href="/bowflex/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Bowflex treadmills guide</a> for the range outside sale weeks.
          </p>
        </div>

